  <static seed="1879" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/FractionAdditionWordProblems20.pg">
    <statement><p>Eric and Jenny are sharing a pizza. Eric ate <m>{{\frac{1}{5}}}</m> of the pizza, and Jenny ate <m>{{\frac{1}{8}}}</m> of the pizza. How much of the pizza was eaten in total?</p>
<p>They ate <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/> of the pizza.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{13}{40}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This is an addition problem.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{1}{5}}} + {{\frac{1}{8}}} 
      \amp = \frac{1 \cdot 8}{5 \cdot 8}+\frac{1 \cdot 5}{8 \cdot 5} \\
      \amp = \frac{8}{40} + \frac{5}{40} \\
      \amp = \frac{8+5}{40} \\
      
      \amp = {{\frac{13}{40}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>They ate <m>{{\frac{13}{40}}}</m> of the pizza.</p>
</solution>
